      "problem": "If $15=x-3$, then $x=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nx-3=15\n$$\n\nTo isolate $x$, we need to perform the *opposite* of subtracting $3$ from $x$, which is *adding* $3$ to $x.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & =15 \\\\ x-3+3 & =15+3 \\\\ x+0 & =18 \\\\ x & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$",
